in any gps receiver , there 's a peak inside that corresponds to the authentic signals .
these three red dots represent the tracking points that try to keep themselves centered on that peak .
but if you send in a fake gps signal , another peak pops up , and if you can get these two peaks perfectly aligned , the tracking points ca n't tell the difference , and they get hijacked by the stronger counterfeit signal , with the authentic peak getting forced off .
at this point , the game is over .
the fake signals now completely control this gps receiver .
